cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bayespk: Bayesian Population Pharmacokinetics Without Writing Stan"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumakura
    given-names: Daiki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9859-0720"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24325845"
    description: "All versions (Zenodo concept DOI)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaikiKumakura/bayespk"
url: "https://daikikumakura.github.io/bayespk/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
abstract: >-
  An R package for Bayesian population pharmacokinetic estimation. The model is described in one line with pk_model() (1- or 2-compartment, IV bolus, infusion or first-order oral absorption, log-normal between-subject variability, covariate formulas, four residual error models), a NONMEM-style data set is passed as it is, and bpk_fit() samples the posterior with precompiled Stan programs that use closed-form solutions. Results include posterior summaries, convergence diagnostics with warnings, prior sensitivity and predictions for new regimens.
keywords:
  - "pharmacometrics"
  - "population pharmacokinetics"
  - "Bayesian"
  - "Stan"
  - "R package"
